Example 1:
Input: s = "abc", t = "ahbgdc"
Output: true

Example 2:
Input: s = "axc", t = "ahbgdc"
Output: false

Code in Python
class Solution:
    def isSubsequence(self, s: str, t: str) -> bool:
        if len(s) == 0:
            return True
        i = 0
        j = 0
        while i<len(s) and j<len(t):
            if s[i] == t[j]:
                i += 1
                j += 1
            else:
                j += 1

        if i!= len(s):
            return False
        else:
            return True


# time complexity is maximum size of the string 't':
o(|t|)
#space complexity o(1) constant only the two variables i and j

#Other approaches
def solve(i, j):
    if i == len(s):
        return True
    if j == len(t):
        return False

    if s[i] == t[j]:
        return solve(i+1, j+1)

    return solve(i, j+1)

Here the time complexity is o(|t1|)
but the space complexity is o(|t1|) because of recursion stack.
